5. **Optimize Your Reads**: Based on the insights from the performance monitoring, identify any inefficient reads and optimize them. This might involve caching data, reducing the amount of data fetched, or restructuring your data to minimize read operations.

6. **Set Up Alerts**: Configure alerts in the Firebase Console to notify you when the number of reads exceeds a certain threshold. This will help you proactively manage and optimize your Firebase usage.

By following these steps, you can effectively instrument your Firebase calls and gain insights into why you have so many reads, allowing you to optimize your app's performance.
